WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.148
NIST Special Publication 800-53 is a catalog of security and privacy controls

00:00:05.148 --> 00:00:08.093
used to help organizations manage cybersecurity risk.

00:00:08.093 --> 00:00:11.879
Developed by the National Institute of Standards and Technology,

00:00:11.879 --> 00:00:17.768
it provides guidance for selecting and implementing safeguards that protect information systems and data.

00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:20.292
Although originally created for federal systems,

00:00:20.292 --> 00:00:24.920
NIST SP 800-53 has influenced security programs across government, critical infrastructure,

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.444
healthcare, education, finance, and commercial industries.

00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:32.913
The key idea is that organizations need a structured way to define safeguards,

00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:37.540
assign responsibility, assess effectiveness, and improve security and privacy over time.
